WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:02.735
-Our next guest is
an Emmy-nominated actress,

00:00:02.735 --> 00:00:04.470
comedian, writer, and producer.

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:06.805
The third season of her
critically-acclaimed show,

00:00:06.805 --> 00:00:09.342
"A Black Lady Sketch Show"
premieres April 8th

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:10.777
on HBO and HBO Max.

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:11.911
Let's take a look.

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:14.114
-Our next comedian has never

00:00:14.114 --> 00:00:17.016
been on Comedy Central
or ComicView.

00:00:17.016 --> 00:00:18.484
why you would write that down?

00:00:18.484 --> 00:00:19.685
I -- Okay.

00:00:19.685 --> 00:00:21.421
Give it up for Keisha.

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:23.389 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:23.389 --> 00:00:24.424
[ Scattered claps ]

00:00:24.424 --> 00:00:26.526
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:28.795
Yesss! How y'all doing?

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:30.829
How y'all doing tonight?
I'm Keisha.

00:00:30.829 --> 00:00:32.965
Y'all look gooder than a Honda
with all its hubcaps.

00:00:32.965 --> 00:00:33.999
[ Laughs ]

00:00:33.999 --> 00:00:35.968
You got a car, ma'am? You rich!

00:00:35.968 --> 00:00:37.737
Oh, what else, what else?

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:39.471
You know I'm just working out
some material.

00:00:39.471 --> 00:00:41.306
Let's see what we got.

00:00:41.306 --> 00:00:42.375
Aw, man, hey. Guess what?

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:44.977
I like my men
like I like my coffee.

00:00:44.977 --> 00:00:46.879
Instant. [ Laughs ]

00:00:46.879 --> 00:00:48.514
Hurry up, sir!

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:50.416
-Please welcome back
to the show,

00:00:50.416 --> 00:00:52.118
our friend Robin Thede,
everyone.

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:53.453
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:53.453 --> 00:00:59.792 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:59.792 --> 00:01:06.165 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:06.165 --> 00:01:12.505 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:14.540
-Welcome back. How are you?
-Hello there.

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:15.941
Hi, everybody.

00:01:15.941 --> 00:01:18.444
-It is very exciting to have
a third season of your show.

00:01:18.444 --> 00:01:19.779
-Listen, you ain't never lied.

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:21.680
Having a third season
of anything.

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:24.384
-I know. In this day and age.
-In this day and age?

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:26.619
-Season three?
Don't mind if you do.

00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:28.621
-Don't mind if I do.

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:30.490
-So Keisha
the stand-up comedian there,

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:33.726
this seems like
a well-observed take

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:36.528
on a kind of stand-up that maybe
nobody is ever happy to see.

00:01:36.528 --> 00:01:38.364
-Yeah. No. I love it.

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:40.200
You know, I started out,
you know this,

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.134
but I started out
writing for comedians.

00:01:42.134 --> 00:01:43.570
In my early days,
I was writing for

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:46.004
Kevin Hart, Anthony Anderson,
all these amazing comedians.

00:01:46.004 --> 00:01:49.408
So I was in the clubs all
the time, and I would see her

00:01:49.408 --> 00:01:52.211
in various iterations,
male, female, whatever.

00:01:52.211 --> 00:01:55.414
And actually, you know,
if you don't --

00:01:55.414 --> 00:01:58.084
I'll just do a little now.

00:01:58.084 --> 00:02:00.119
[ As Keisha ] Hey,
how y'all doing tonight?

00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:01.120
Hey!

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:02.321
[ Applause ]
No, don't clap.

00:02:02.321 --> 00:02:04.023
Don't clap.
She's terrible. She's terrible.

00:02:04.023 --> 00:02:05.324
[ As Keisha ]
How y'all doing? Hey!

00:02:05.324 --> 00:02:06.325
What's your sweater?

00:02:06.325 --> 00:02:08.193
Sad? Because it's blue.

00:02:08.193 --> 00:02:09.795
[ Laughs ]

00:02:09.795 --> 00:02:11.497
What else?

00:02:11.497 --> 00:02:12.498
-The speed!

00:02:12.498 --> 00:02:14.701
-This is a person
that when she --

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:16.503
I don't know why I'm using this.

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:20.372
What the person would yell,
like, the key to their comedy

00:02:20.372 --> 00:02:22.809
was just yelling
the explanation of the joke.

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:25.377
So it's like, "Your sweater
is blue 'cause it's sad.

00:02:25.377 --> 00:02:27.280
It's blue!

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:29.382
'Cause it's sad.
[ Laughs ] Get it?"

00:02:29.382 --> 00:02:33.986
That person, the more you yell

00:02:33.986 --> 00:02:36.522
the explanation of the joke,
it doesn't help.

00:02:36.522 --> 00:02:38.557
-It seems like a lot of
characters on this show

00:02:38.557 --> 00:02:40.894
must be people that you have
observed in real life.

00:02:40.894 --> 00:02:41.894
-Yeah.

00:02:41.894 --> 00:02:42.962
-Is that something
you're always --

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:43.963
do you feel like
you have a good radar

00:02:43.963 --> 00:02:45.931
for who might be
a character inspiration?

00:02:45.931 --> 00:02:47.634
-Well, I definitely
steal it from

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:49.468
any and everyone
I can, that's for sure.

00:02:49.468 --> 00:02:53.506
I am watching people constantly,
like a creeper,

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:56.109
and listening to them
all the time.

00:02:56.109 --> 00:02:57.509
but it has gotten me in trouble.

00:02:57.509 --> 00:02:58.944
-You have gotten
caught creeping?

00:02:58.944 --> 00:03:01.214
-Oh, yeah.
-Really? Wow.

00:03:01.214 --> 00:03:05.651
-Okay, I was at the car wash
and a guy walks past me.

00:03:05.651 --> 00:03:06.953
I have my head down,
I'm on my phone,

00:03:06.953 --> 00:03:09.355
and I hear him go,
"You are so beautiful."

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:10.823
I look up and I go,
"Thank you."

00:03:10.823 --> 00:03:13.392
and he goes, [Whispering]
"I'm on the phone.

00:03:13.392 --> 00:03:16.762
I'm on the phone."

00:03:16.762 --> 00:03:18.998
So, you know, that wasn't even
me observing characters.

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:20.799
-That was just eavesdropping.

00:03:20.799 --> 00:03:23.803
-Absorbing compliments
that weren't mine.

00:03:23.803 --> 00:03:25.905
-You have so
many great guest stars,

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:27.139
which you had in
the first couple seasons,

00:03:27.139 --> 00:03:28.541
but more than ever.

00:03:28.541 --> 00:03:31.177
A nice mix of comedy guest stars
that I'm assuming

00:03:31.177 --> 00:03:32.745
show up and you know exactly
what you're going to get.

00:03:32.745 --> 00:03:35.547
And then a lot of dramatic
actors as well.

00:03:35.547 --> 00:03:37.483
Do you get a little nervous
not knowing

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:39.385
how funny they're going to be
until they show up on set?

00:03:39.385 --> 00:03:40.653
-You know what's crazy?

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:43.389
This season we have over
40 celebrity guest stars.

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:44.824
You guys are going to love it.

00:03:44.824 --> 00:03:46.259
-That is amazing.
-It's crazy.

00:03:46.259 --> 00:03:47.793
In six episodes.

00:03:47.793 --> 00:03:49.261
-What's your bar,
though, for famous?

00:03:49.261 --> 00:03:50.563
-Wanda Sykes.

00:03:50.563 --> 00:03:51.597
Hello?
-That's very famous.

00:03:51.597 --> 00:03:53.265
-David Alan Grier.
Tommy Davidson.

00:03:53.265 --> 00:03:54.801
-Very impressive.
-All these amazing people.

00:03:54.801 --> 00:03:58.103
Then we have the drama actors,
also, like Vanessa Williams,

00:03:58.103 --> 00:04:01.874
Lance Reddick, Michaela Jae
Rodriguez from "Pose,"

00:04:01.874 --> 00:04:03.342
Michael Ealy.

00:04:03.342 --> 00:04:06.546
So many amazing, amazing
dramatic actors.

00:04:06.546 --> 00:04:08.113
And you would think that
when they'd get on set

00:04:08.113 --> 00:04:10.683
they would be like,
"What is my motivation?"

00:04:10.683 --> 00:04:12.218
But they're not.
They're the goofiest ones.

00:04:12.218 --> 00:04:13.352
Lance Reddick.

00:04:13.352 --> 00:04:14.620
-That makes me so happy.
-Oh, my God.

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:16.622
He was just like, "Please,
just give me more jokes."

00:04:16.622 --> 00:04:18.290
They love it.

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:21.393
-It must be so liberating
compared to, you know,

00:04:21.393 --> 00:04:23.629
especially when somebody
like Lance Reddick,

00:04:23.629 --> 00:04:26.032
who's oftentimes
doing really dark material.

00:04:26.032 --> 00:04:27.867
It must be so fun.
-Yeah, this isn't "The Wire."

00:04:27.867 --> 00:04:31.637
You're good.
You can let loose a little bit.

00:04:31.637 --> 00:04:33.106
The funny thing is, you know,

00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:35.108
so we'll do the script as
written.

00:04:35.108 --> 00:04:38.311
Our Emmy-nominated writers.

00:04:38.311 --> 00:04:40.446
-Of course.
You have to do it as written.

00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:42.782
-You have to do it as written,
because they're very sensitive.

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:44.216
And by they, I mean me.

00:04:44.216 --> 00:04:47.153
So we do it as scripted,

00:04:47.153 --> 00:04:49.021
but then we're like,
"Okay, rip up the script.

00:04:49.021 --> 00:04:50.122
Now do whatever you want.

00:04:50.122 --> 00:04:51.323
And they just kind of
look at you

00:04:51.323 --> 00:04:52.492
like a deer in headlights.

00:04:52.492 --> 00:04:54.360
They're like, "What do you mean,
whatever I want?"

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:55.427
I'm like, "Just say any words.
It's fine.

00:04:55.427 --> 00:04:56.495
You know the story."

00:04:56.495 --> 00:04:58.297
And they're the best at it,
actually.

00:04:58.297 --> 00:04:59.498
-That's wonderful.

00:04:59.498 --> 00:05:02.267
I imagine because you have
been so successful

00:05:02.267 --> 00:05:04.169
getting people to do your show,

00:05:04.169 --> 00:05:06.372
that now people pitch to you
all the time other people

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:07.473
who you should go out and ask.

00:05:07.473 --> 00:05:10.343
-They do.
They do, which sometimes works,

00:05:10.343 --> 00:05:12.611
if the person is someone
that I feel like we can get.

00:05:12.611 --> 00:05:14.413
My mom is constantly pitching,

00:05:14.413 --> 00:05:16.382
"Why don't you
have Beyonce on the show?"

00:05:16.382 --> 00:05:18.150
-That's a good idea.

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:20.119
-One of my other friends is
like, "Janet Jackson.

00:05:20.119 --> 00:05:21.821
Just get Janet Jackson."

00:05:21.821 --> 00:05:25.157
-Why don't you listen
to these good ideas?

00:05:25.157 --> 00:05:29.428
-Listen, Janet Jackson, Beyonce,
Blue Ivy, Sir, Rumi, any of you,

00:05:29.428 --> 00:05:31.030
please, come on the show.

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:33.098
-I have terrible news.
They don't watch this show.

00:05:33.098 --> 00:05:35.735
-They don't.
They definitely don't.

00:05:35.735 --> 00:05:37.369
Some of them are way
too young to be watching.

00:05:37.369 --> 00:05:38.738
-I didn't know about this.

00:05:38.738 --> 00:05:41.440
I read this, that you were
named after Robin Williams.

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:43.875
-I was.
-So that says to me that

00:05:43.875 --> 00:05:45.010
comedy must have been

00:05:45.010 --> 00:05:46.312
an important part
of your upbringing.

00:05:46.312 --> 00:05:47.547
Your parents
obviously valued it,

00:05:47.547 --> 00:05:48.680
if they named you
after Robin Williams.

00:05:48.680 --> 00:05:50.015
That must have been
a really cool thing.

00:05:50.015 --> 00:05:52.384
-Or I look very different now
than I did as a baby,

00:05:52.384 --> 00:05:53.686
if I resembled him.

00:05:53.686 --> 00:05:54.753
I'm not sure.

00:05:54.753 --> 00:05:56.255
-You were born in suspenders.

00:05:56.255 --> 00:06:00.526
-I was. I was. Oh, my God.

00:06:00.526 --> 00:06:02.862
I think they were just watching
"Mork &amp; Mindy" when I was born.

00:06:02.862 --> 00:06:04.630
I don't know.

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:06.832
It was like, a real bonding time
for my dad and I.

00:06:06.832 --> 00:06:10.102
We would watch "SNL" right up
until Weekend Update.

00:06:10.102 --> 00:06:12.171
That was, you know,
I was like, 5.

00:06:12.171 --> 00:06:13.439
And so it was like,

00:06:13.439 --> 00:06:14.806
"Alright, you've got to
go to bed at that time."

00:06:14.806 --> 00:06:17.075
But, yeah,
he loved Robin Williams.

00:06:17.075 --> 00:06:18.845
He was such a massive fan,
but who isn't?

00:06:18.845 --> 00:06:20.112
-Of course.

00:06:20.112 --> 00:06:24.617
-But he loved him with such
unbridled passion.

00:06:24.617 --> 00:06:26.385
-As a kid, then,
did that give you --

00:06:26.385 --> 00:06:29.422
were you sort of encouraged
to do sketch comedy?

00:06:29.422 --> 00:06:31.290
Did they like
watching you goof around?

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:33.225
-They definitely
didn't not encourage it.

00:06:33.225 --> 00:06:35.127
I would be watching
the local news

00:06:35.127 --> 00:06:37.763
and the news anchor would say,
"Tonight, our top story,"

00:06:37.763 --> 00:06:39.932
and I would go,
"Tonight, our top story."

00:06:39.932 --> 00:06:41.467
They're like,
"What is she doing?"

00:06:41.467 --> 00:06:42.901
And then they would laugh,
and I'm like,

00:06:42.901 --> 00:06:44.470
"Oh, wait, I'm getting laughs."

00:06:44.470 --> 00:06:45.738
And so, yeah.

00:06:45.738 --> 00:06:48.540
I would start mimicking
everything I saw on TV.

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:50.075
-Well, it paid off.

00:06:50.075 --> 00:06:51.144
They have a lot to be proud of.

00:06:51.144 --> 00:06:52.611
Congratulations, again.
-Thank you.

00:06:52.611 --> 00:06:54.413
-Three seasons.
-Yes!

00:06:54.413 --> 00:06:55.414
[ Cheers and applause ]
-This is the best one yet!

00:06:55.414 --> 00:06:57.449
You guys, that's Robin Thede.

00:06:57.449 --> 00:06:58.984
The third season of
"A Black Lady Sketch Show"

00:06:58.984 --> 00:07:01.521
premieres April 8th
on HBO and HBO Max.

